 using a text message when the caller is a contact calling from a mobile phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071247">text reply</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084440">yi amsa da saƙo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36790_2071376_2084429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A camera option to capture just one image when the user presses the camera button.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071376">single photo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084429">hoto guda</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36791_2071377_2375961"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo you can choose to use as the background for some Live Tiles on the Start screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071377">Start background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2375961">Bayanbangon Farawa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36792_2071378_2084454"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows Phone feature to upgrade a phone call into a Skype video call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071378">video upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084454">ɗagawa darajar bidiyo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36793_2071379_2084460"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that enables app screen content to display in a window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071379">windowed mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084460">yanayin taga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36794_2071380_2084401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that is similar to “stretch” - the resolution of the phone screen is refitted to fill as much of the external screen as possible without compromising its dimensionality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071380">expanded screen mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084401">yanayin faɗaɗɗen allo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36795_2071381_2084421"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows desktop application that is required to enable users to project their phone screen to a Windows device using a USB connection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071381">Project My Screen App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2084421">Manahajar Bayyana Allon Waje</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2072311_2085128"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072311">Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote><