ated by digital cameras.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2412466">Digital Negative</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414113">DNG</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42581_2412468_2414065"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual effect that occurs when a photo is taken of a fast-moving object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2412468">motion blur</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414065">dushewar motsi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42582_2412469_2414114"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that initiates a 2, 5, or 10-second delay for taking a picture.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2412469">photo timer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414114">mai ƙirga lokacin hoto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42582_2905571_2414114"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that initiates a 2, 5, or 10-second delay for taking a picture.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2905571">timer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414114">mai ƙirga lokacin hoto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42607_2413500_2420849"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office button that launches a task pane where users can research papers by typing queries to get information such as sources, citations, quotes, and images.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2413500">Researcher</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2420849">Maibincike</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42608_2413506_2420850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office feature that allows users type queries and find information, sources, citations, quotes, and images, without leaving the application that they are using.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2413506">Researcher</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2420850">Maibincike</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42614_2414369_2417505"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">T​o quickly return to an app, website, or document you were using earlier.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414369">jump back</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417505">tsallake baya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42615_2414370_2417506"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of documents, apps, and websites that, in one click, allows you to pick up your work exactly where you left it earlier, on any device connected with the same Microsoft account.​​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414370">jump group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417506">rukunin tsallake</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42616_2414371_2417504"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To quickly jump to a document or application on another device that is connected to the same Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414371">jump</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417504">tsallake</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42617_2414373_2417507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lets customers reset their network settings back to the Windows defaults.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414373">network reset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417507">sake saiti na hanyar sadarwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">NGA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42639_2414859_2417508"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control that contains a customizable and extensible collection of ink-related features for Universal Windows apps. By default, the toolbar may include buttons for drawing, erasing, highlighting, setting ink color and stroke thickness, and displaying a ruler.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2414859">Windows Ink toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ha-Latn-NG"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417508">Tulba na Windows Ink</term><termNote type="geograp